# fps validation is done by the video output (not by the early size check of obs_reset_video): a zero
# denominator is rejected only after the previous video state was torn down, and the result is the
# generic failure code (the invalid-parameter code of the output is swallowed by mix creation).
# A zero numerator crashes the reference (division by zero while computing the frame interval, see
# D-2); it is probed in a forked child: a conforming implementation must instead return invalid_param
# (the probe line shows the reference result).
startup en-US -
reset_video
video_info
reset_video fps=30/0
video_info
state
probe_reset_video fps=0/1
probe_reset_video fps=0/0
reset_video fps=30000/1001
video_info
intervals
reset_video fps=60/1
intervals
reset_video fps=1/3
intervals
reset_video fps=1000000000/1
intervals
shutdown
